  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "• Boil the kettle. Half-fill a medium saucepan with boiling water.\n• Cook egg noodles over medium-high heat, stirring occasionally with a fork to separate, until tender, 4-5 minutes. Drain, rinse and set aside.\n• Meanwhile, slice carrot and zucchini into half-moons.\n• Cut Japanese tofu into bite-sized chunks.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/6374895cf2957726d00103b1/step-a60b0816.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• In a medium bowl, combine tofu, cornflour, the salt and a pinch of pepper.\n• In a large frying pan, heat a generous drizzle of olive oil over medium-high heat. When oil is hot, shake excess flour off tofu and cook, tossing, until browned, 3-4 minutes.\n• Transfer tofu to a paper towel-lined plate. Cover to keep warm.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/6374895cf2957726d00103b1/step-386a99b2.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• Wipe out frying pan, then return pan to high heat with a drizzle of olive oil. Cook carrot and zucchini until tender, 4-5 minutes.\n• Add ginger paste and cook until fragrant, 1 minute.\n• Stir in katsu paste, coconut milk and the soy sauce until combined and heated through, 2-3 minutes.\n• Add cooked noodles and the baby spinach leaves. Cook, stirring, until spinach is wilted, 1 minute.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/6374895cf2957726d00103b1/step-1dcbb2df.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• Divide curried egg noodles and crispy tofu between bowls.\n• Drizzle with sweet chilli sauce. Sprinkle with crispy shallots to serve. Enjoy!",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/6374895cf2957726d00103b1/step-a8191bbf.jpg"
    }
  ]
